# No private-repo references in this public repo

`bayesimpact/bayes-platform` is **public**. Anything written here is world-readable: commits, PR titles/bodies, comments, code, docs, changelogs, branch names that spell a private repo, CI logs you paste into PRs.

## Forbidden in this repository

Never put any of the following into commits, PRs, comments, docs, code, or changelogs:

- Links or names of **private** GitHub repos (especially `bayesimpact/internal-issues`)
- `Closes` / `Fixes` / `Refs` / `Part of` trailers that point at a private repo issue
  (e.g. `Closes bayesimpact/internal-issues#137`, `Refs: bayesimpact/internal-issues#137`)
- Internal-only URLs, tickets, or tracker IDs that only resolve inside a private org repo

Tracking a private security/internal issue is fine **in chat with the user**. Do **not** mirror that reference into the public git history or GitHub UI.

## What to write instead

- Describe the change on its own (no private issue link).
- If a public bayes-platform issue exists, link that (`Closes #1234`).
- If work was driven by a private issue only, omit the reference entirely.

```
# ❌ BAD — leaks a private tracker into the public repo
Closes bayesimpact/internal-issues#137
Refs: bayesimpact/internal-issues#137

# ✅ GOOD — no private tracker
# (no Closes/Refs line, or Closes #<public bayes-platform issue>)
```

## Before every commit and `gh pr create` / `gh pr edit`

Scan the message/body for `internal-issues`, other private repo slugs, and `bayesimpact/` links that are not `bayesimpact/bayes-platform`. Remove them before committing or publishing.
